---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How this site is built" description="A static Astro site built and deployed by GitHub Actions to GitHub Pages.">
  <h1>How this site is built</h1>
  <p class="lede">A small static site: plain HTML generated by Astro, built and deployed automatically on every change.</p>

  <svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 760 120" role="img" aria-label="Pipeline: a git push to GitHub triggers GitHub Actions, which builds the Astro site and deploys it to GitHub Pages, which serves visitors over HTTPS.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="currentColor" style="color:var(--muted)" />
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <rect class="box" x="10" y="30" width="150" height="56" rx="10" />
    <text x="85" y="55" text-anchor="middle">git push</text>
    <text x="85" y="73" text-anchor="middle" class="label">content in code</text>

    <rect class="box" x="210" y="30" width="150" height="56" rx="10" />
    <text x="285" y="55" text-anchor="middle">GitHub Actions</text>
    <text x="285" y="73" text-anchor="middle" class="label">Astro build</text>

    <rect class="box" x="410" y="30" width="150" height="56" rx="10" />
    <text x="485" y="55" text-anchor="middle">GitHub Pages</text>
    <text x="485" y="73" text-anchor="middle" class="label">CDN · HTTPS</text>

    <rect class="box" x="610" y="30" width="140" height="56" rx="10" />
    <text x="680" y="55" text-anchor="middle">Visitor</text>
    <text x="680" y="73" text-anchor="middle" class="label">browser</text>

    <path class="edge" d="M160 58 H205" />
    <path class="edge" d="M360 58 H405" />
    <path class="edge" d="M560 58 H605" />
  </svg>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Components</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Astro</strong> generates plain static HTML, so there is no server to run or patch.</li>
      <li><strong>Content as data:</strong> profile details and case studies live in two small TypeScript files, so updates are one-line changes.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub Actions</strong> builds the site on every push to the main branch.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> serves it over HTTPS from a global CDN.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cost</h2>
    <p>Hosting is free. A custom domain, if used, is the only cost.</p>

    <h2>Also ready for AWS</h2>
    <p>The repository includes Terraform for an AWS version of the same site: a private S3 bucket behind CloudFront with HTTPS, Route 53 DNS, a budget alert, and a GitHub deploy role that uses OpenID Connect instead of stored keys.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
